# texts.rec: every line of dialogue, book and quest text, by id. quests.rec, objects and townspeople say them.
# %rec: text
#   id                the text's id (TEXT_...); required
#   text              the words; they continue on lines that start with "+ ", and a line of just "+" starts a paragraph
#   sfx               voices.rec id spoken with it (none: silent)
#   gossip            the townsperson (internal name) who may say it as gossip; their gossip goes in file order,
#                     the greeting first
#
# Heaven & Hell's town dialogue, from main's files/assets/dialogue/*.txt. This game has no speech, so no sfx.
# A line of just "+" starts a new paragraph. quests.rec decides who says what, when.

%rec: text

id: TEXT_HH_KIRIOTH_WELCOME
text: Welcome, my friend!
+
+ I am Kirioth, the eldest of this town.
+
+ You've come at the right time. Our town is under attack by demons and the living dead.
+
+ Please, enter the cathedral to the north-east of town and end this madness.
+
+ There is one particular dangerous demon on the second level of the cathedral.
+
+ You must defeat him to save our town!

id: TEXT_HH_KIRIOTH_MEAT_JACK
text: Please, that unholy abomination is still waiting on the second floor of the cathedral.
+
+ Hurry, before it's too late.

id: TEXT_HH_KIRIOTH_MEAT_JACK_REWARD
text: You've done us a great service, friend. Here, take this. It's the least I can do to thank you.

id: TEXT_HH_KIRIOTH_AFTER_MEAT_JACK
text: Thanks again, for helping us make this town safer for everyone.

id: TEXT_HH_KIRIOTH_LUCIFER_QUEST
text: It's all clear now.
+
+ It's him, it's always been him.
+
+ Beneath our very feet lies the answer to all our questions.
+
+ You must travel the caves that are located under the catacombs.
+
+ Find the entrance to hell itself and slay the devil.

id: TEXT_HH_KIRIOTH_LUCIFER_QUEST_REWARD
text: You've done it!
+
+ You've really done it!
+
+ Here, take this as an unworthy reward.

id: TEXT_HH_SHEKEL_WELCOME
text: Welcome, my friend!
+
+ I am Shekel, the leader of the merchants' guild.
+
+ These demons have been a plague on our town for some days now. It's getting worse by the hour.
+
+ Business has been slow, and customers are afraid to even enter the town.
+
+ I am currently investigating the source of this evil.
+
+ Come back later, and I will tell you what I have found.

id: TEXT_HH_SHEKEL_SKELETON_KING_QUEST
text: Ah, you've come at the right time.
+
+ My sources tell me, that the evil king Zedek has returned from the dead.
+
+ His tomb is on the fourth level, inside the catacombs.
+
+ You must find him and his devilish undead minions and destroy them once and for all.
+
+ Good luck, brave adventurer.

id: TEXT_HH_SHEKEL_SKELETON_KING_QUEST_REWARD
text: You've done well, my friend. You've done well.
+
+ Here is your reward.

id: TEXT_HH_SHEKEL_AFTER_SKELETON_KING
text: We owe you so much!

id: TEXT_HH_ABEL_WELCOME
text: Welcome, my brother!
+
+ I am Abel.
+
+ Bad things are happening in this town. I am sure you have heard of the abduction of Shekel's son Jim?
+
+ When you have dealt with the immediate threat, I have a request for you.
+
+ Please, kill that abomination that has been terrorizing our townsfolk.

id: TEXT_HH_ABEL_POISON_QUEST
text: Thanks for dealing with that monster.
+
+ There's still an issue of utmost importance that needs to be addressed.
+
+ For some weeks now our rivers have been polluted by a mysterious substance.
+
+ There are rumors that it's coming from the catacombs.
+
+ Please, find out what's going on. If there are any monsters down there, defeat them, and you'll be rewarded.

id: TEXT_HH_ABEL_POISON_QUEST_REWARD
text: You've been a great help.
+
+ Please, take this reward.

id: TEXT_HH_ABEL_AFTER_POISON_QUEST
text: Thanks for cleaning up the water.

id: TEXT_HH_MARY_WELCOME
text: Welcome, stranger.
+
+ I am sister Mary.

id: TEXT_HH_LUCIFER_DEATH
text: These bones may be broken, but my spirit can't die. We'll meet again.
+
+ I will find you, should you someday decide to bring righteous vengeance to the true source of evil in this world.
+
+ I will allow you to try this again.
+
+ You will find a gift of mine, when you return to your cozy little town. It might help open your eyes.

# Lucifer's note, left with his gift (main's note_lucifer.txt, which nothing loaded): it opens the evidence quest.

id: TEXT_HH_NOTE_LUCIFER
text: Congratulations, for now you are among the seeing.
+
+ Look at the world around you again. Then come and find me.
+
+ Oh, one last thing. You can attack EVERYONE with a "SHIFT" of your attention.
+
+ - The Morningstar

# The evidence notes, one for each of plan.txt's "crimes of the people". main only had a placeholder for them.

id: TEXT_HH_NOTE_EVIDENCE_ONE
text: Report of the waterworks crew, for the Union.
+
+ The sickness did not come up from the caves. We traced it to the barrels from Master Shekel's potion works, poured into the cistern by night while his own guards kept watch.
+
+ By morning the criers blamed the Union for the foul water. Three of our brothers hang in the square for it.
+
+ Whoever finds this: the poison is Shekel's.

id: TEXT_HH_NOTE_EVIDENCE_TWO
text: I, Zedek, king of this land, set down my last will while I still can.
+
+ My counsellor Kirioth whispers to my brother, and Abel no longer meets my eyes. I fear a knife in the dark.
+
+ Should I fall by my brother's hand, let it be known that the crown was stolen, not inherited, and that my people owe the thief nothing.

id: TEXT_HH_NOTE_EVIDENCE_THREE
text: Kept in case the old man ever forgets who his friends are. - S.
+
+ K. promised: the crown for Abel, the waterworks and the potion trade for me, and for himself the power beneath the town.
+
+ He took twelve of the poor from the lower quarter down to the old cathedral. None came back. That night the ground shook, and K. spoke of a prince he had called up and would bind to his will.
+
+ He did not bind it.

id: TEXT_HH_NOTE_EVIDENCE_FOUR
text: S.,
+
+ The laboratory in the caves is ready. Send the next subjects down by the kitchen stairs, as before.
+
+ So far: seven dead, two fled, one kept. Your boy survived the treatment. He is stronger than ten men now, and always hungry.
+
+ Tell his mother it was the fever. - K.

# Lucifer keeps his word once the evidence is in (plan.txt's "Lucifer's Rant").

id: TEXT_HH_LUCIFER_RANT
text: So you still don't understand, do you?
+
+ Think about it. What is the reason you are unable to defeat me? Or any human in the centuries before?
+
+ It's simple, really. You are fighting a mere idea, a concept you brought to life yourself.
+
+ And for what pitiful reason did you invent me? As a scapegoat for all your own evil deeds. Like a child, you blame me for what is really your own fault.
+
+ Look around you and open your eyes to the truth. The true enemy of mankind is, and always has been, mankind itself.

# The second act (plan.txt's "Quests #2"): Lucifer, in the town in hell, sends the hero after the town's true
# villains. Drafted by Claude from plan.txt; not yet reviewed.

id: TEXT_HH_LUCIFER_ACT2_OFFER
text: So your eyes are open at last. Good.
+
+ Then let us settle the town's accounts. Four debts are owed, and three can be collected now.
+
+ The adventurers who came down after you butcher everything they meet on the ninth level, and they call it heroism. End them.
+
+ King Zedek's army still marches because their king was never laid to rest. Shekel keeps his crown as a trophy in his house. Take it back and bury it in his tomb.
+
+ And Shekel himself, the man who poisoned the water and blamed the workers, hides in the merchant district below. He will not see you coming.

id: TEXT_HH_LUCIFER_ACT2_WAITING
text: The adventurers on the ninth level, Zedek's crown, Shekel in the merchant district. The debts are still open.

id: TEXT_HH_LUCIFER_ADVENTURERS_DONE
text: Four fewer heroes. The ninth level is quiet, and nobody up there will mourn them.

id: TEXT_HH_LUCIFER_SKELETON_ARMY_DONE
text: The dead king rests, and his army with him. They were the only ones in that town who kept their oaths.

id: TEXT_HH_LUCIFER_SHEKEL_DONE
text: Shekel is dead. The water will stay clean now, and the workers will never know who to thank.

id: TEXT_HH_LUCIFER_KIRIOTH_OFFER
text: One debt remains, and it is the largest.
+
+ Kirioth. He turned a prince against his king, sold a boy to Shekel's experiments, and fed the poor to the ritual that summoned me, thinking he could hold my leash.
+
+ He waits for you in town. When you arrive, he will finally show you his true face. Finish it.

id: TEXT_HH_LUCIFER_KIRIOTH_WAITING
text: Kirioth still breathes. Go to town.

id: TEXT_HH_KIRIOTH_DEATH
text: You... were supposed to be my hero.

id: TEXT_HH_LUCIFER_ENDING
text: It is done. The town is free of the men who ruled it, and no one will ever call you a hero for it.
+
+ Now you understand what I have always been: the one they blame. Walk with me, and we will see how long the next ones last.

id: TEXT_HH_ZEDEK_CROWN
text: A king's crown, dented where a blade struck it from behind. It belongs in King Zedek's tomb, on the fourth level.

id: TEXT_HH_ZEDEK_CROWN_BURIED
text: You lay the crown in the dust of King Zedek's tomb. Somewhere below, a thousand bones settle at once.
